{"slug": "tahini-ramen-salad", "nyt_id": 1024037, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024037-tahini-ramen-salad", "name": "Tahini Ramen Salad", "author": "Kay Chun", "description": "A breeze to make on busy weeknights, this fresh, colorful ramen salad is equally tasty at room temperature or chilled — which means it’s particularly picnic-friendly. Chickpeas add creamy texture, contrasting the crisp bite of vibrant veggies. Use your favorite combination: Yellow bell peppers, cucumbers, snap peas, radishes, celery, asparagus and cabbage are all great options. You can make the salad an hour ahead and let the savory tahini-garlic sauce soak into the noodles (at room temperature); just give it a quick toss before serving so that everything is evenly coated in the luscious sauce. If chilled, pull the salad from the refrigerator 10 minutes before serving to allow the sauce to soften, then give it a nice mix.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 20, "cook_minutes": 10, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"prep": "PT20M", "cook": "PT10M", "total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "12 ounces dry ramen noodles (or four 3-ounce individual packages, seasoning packets discarded or reserved for another use)", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "dry ramen noodles (or four 3-ounce individual packages", "preparation": "seasoning packets discarded or reserved for another use)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 tablespoons tahini", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tahini", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "6 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup distilled white vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "distilled white vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons sweet miso", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sweet miso", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 tablespoon minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Kosher salt and black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt and black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 (15-ounce) can chickpeas, rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "can", "item": "chickpeas", "preparation": "rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "4 cups thinly sliced vegetables (such as yellow bell pepper, cucumbers, radishes and snap peas)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced vegetables (such as yellow bell pepper", "preparation": "cucumbers, radishes and snap peas)", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup thinly sliced scallions", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced scallions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a medium pot of boiling water, cook the ramen noodles according to package directions until al dente. Drain, rinse under cold water until cool, then drain well; transfer to a large bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a small bowl, combine tahini, oil, vinegar, ginger, miso, garlic and ¼ cup of water. Season with salt and pepper and whisk until smooth."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add ½ cup of the dressing to the noodles, season and toss to coat. Add chickpeas, sliced vegetables, scallions and remaining dressing; season and toss to coat. Serve at room temperature or chilled."}], "nu